Backport of apache/arrow f9315d4e7 (GH-49565, PR #49567), first released
in arrow 24.0.0. Cython >= 3.3 emits cython_std::move<T>(x) with an
explicit template argument, so T no longer deduces to a const reference
and neither move(T&) nor move(T&&) binds the const parameter:

  _parquet_encryption.cpp: error: no matching function for call to 'move'
  note: candidate ... 1st argument ('const parquet::encryption::KmsConnectionConfig')
        would lose const qualifier

Copy into a non-const local first, as upstream does.

diff --git a/python/pyarrow/_parquet_encryption.pyx b/python/pyarrow/_parquet_encryption.pyx
--- a/python/pyarrow/_parquet_encryption.pyx
+++ b/python/pyarrow/_parquet_encryption.pyx
@@ -296,7 +296,10 @@
     @staticmethod
     cdef wrap(const CKmsConnectionConfig& config):
         result = KmsConnectionConfig()
-        result.configuration = make_shared[CKmsConnectionConfig](move(config))
+        # We require a copy of the config because the input is
+        # a const reference owned by C++.
+        cdef CKmsConnectionConfig config_copy = config
+        result.configuration = make_shared[CKmsConnectionConfig](move(config_copy))
         return result
 
 
